gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.46826db6d1e97a725b85504d8a9426472b687ccb.001.1"},{"event":"Hydrologic Outlook","headline":"Hydrologic Outlook issued October 9 at 10:53AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"ESFGJT\n\nA strong low pressure system off the Pacific Coast will begin to draw\nin tropical moisture associated with Topical Storm Rachel this\nweekend. This strong southerly fetch will draw anomalously high\nmoisture content across the Desert Southwest and into eastern Utah\nand western Colorado. The chance for widespread precipitation\nincreases Saturday evening into Sunday. Total precipitation forecasts\nrange from 1 to 3 inches across high terrain, with highest amounts\nfavoring the Uintas, Tavaputs and the Southwest San Juan mountains.\n\nEmbedded thunderstorms are also possible Sunday afternoon, increasing\nthe threat for flash flooding across vulnerable terrain. While\nconfidence in location and rainfall rates remain low at this time,\nthe potential for rapidly rising rivers, streams, normally dry\narroyos and slot canyons are possible Sunday through Monday.\n\nPlease follow the evolving forecast, especially if your plans\nincluding recreating or commuting across eastern Utah and western\nColorado Sunday onward. Also, keep in mind weather potential above\nyour location and upstream, particularly for those who reside below\nsensitive terrain like recent burn scars.","ends":"2026-10-12T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Delta, CO; Dolores, CO; Garfield, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Mesa, CO; Moffat, CO; Montezuma, CO; Montrose, CO; Ouray, CO; Rio Blanco, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Daggett, UT; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT; Uintah, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-11T06:00:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 110600 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1200 AM MDT Sun Oct 11 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Deep moisture continues through the weekend as remnants of tropical system Rachel move through the region, especially overnight and through Sunday. Rainfall totals of 2-3 inches are possible over the eastern Utah mountains and 1-2 inches across the San Ju","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-11T09:00:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Widespread wetting rains will continue across the region today, as extra-tropical moisture moves across the region. Some strong thunderstorms are expected to develop with damaging winds, hail, and heavy rainfall. Flash flooding remains a concern around sensitive terrain. Winds will increase appreciably today, gusting to around 45 mph across much of eastern UT and western CO. Critica","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"frt03","station_name":"CSU Fruita Exp Station","distance_km":3.8,"soil_temp_5cm_f":63.45,"soil_temp_15cm_f":65.39,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":0,"wind_speed_mph":5.9,"air_temp_f":56.21,"relative_humidity":0.906,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/frt03"},"aviation":{"icao":"KGJT","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KGJT 110853Z AUTO 11014KT 10SM FEW055 OVC085 14/12 A2988 RMK AO2 RAB0756E10 SLP070 P0000 60005 T01390117 58010","temp_f":57,"wind_dir":110,"wind_kt":14,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"OVC","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1011.9,"observed":1791708780,"raw_taf":"TAF KGJT 110540Z 1106/1206 10012KT P6SM -SHRA BKN060 OVC090 TEMPO 1106/1110 4SM -SHRA BR OVC035 FM111000 12015G25KT P6SM -SHRA OVC045 PROB30 1112/1117 4SM -SHRA BR OVC025 FM111700 15017G28KT P6SM VCSH SCT050 BKN080 PROB30 1117/1122 VR